.TH LAMP 1 "2026-08-05" "lamp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lamp \- control the Mi Bedside Lamp 2 over the local network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lamp
[\fIargument\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Controls a Mi Bedside Lamp 2 (MJCTD02YL) directly over the miIO protocol on
udp/54321. Everything happens on the local network: there is no cloud round
trip, no hub, and no dependency on the Xiaomi or Yeelight apps. The lamp's
HomeKit pairing is untouched, so the Home app keeps working alongside it.
.PP
Setting a brightness or colour on a lamp that is off will also turn it on.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B (none)
Toggle power.
.TP
.BR on ", " off
Set power directly.
.TP
.B <0-100>
Set brightness as a percentage. A value of 0 turns the lamp off.
.TP
.BI <n> k
Set colour temperature in kelvin, for example
.BR "lamp 2700k" .
Values are clamped to the 1700\-6500K the device accepts. The
.B k
suffix is required, so that brightness and temperature cannot be confused.
.TP
.BR warm ", " cool
Shorthand for 2700k and 5000k.
.TP
.BI # rrggbb
Set colour. The leading hash is optional.
.TP
.BI @ scene
Apply a named scene from the configuration file.
.TP
.B status
Print power, brightness, and current colour or temperature. Also reports how
long a manual override still has to run.
.SH AUTOMATION
Any command typed by hand claims the lamp for two hours, or until
.B lamp off
is run. The reconciler leaves it alone for that long, so automation can never
undo something done deliberately.
.TP
.B auto
Hand control back to the reconciler immediately.
.TP
.B tick
Apply the rules once. This is what the launch agent runs; it prints nothing and
exits zero when there is nothing to do.
.TP
.BR "agent on" ", " "agent off"
Install or remove the launch agent that runs
.B tick
every 30 seconds.
.SH RULES
The reconciler decides brightness and colour from three inputs, and
.B never turns the lamp on
\(em it only adjusts a lamp that is already on, so it cannot light an empty
room. An unreachable lamp is a silent no-op.
.TP
.B Time of day
The schedule sets the brightness baseline. The slot in force is the last one to
have started, wrapping around midnight.
.TP
.B Media
While any audio is playing, brightness is capped at
.IR media.brightness .
This only ever dims; it will not brighten a lamp the schedule has taken down
for the night.
.TP
.B Theme
The accent colour of the active swatch theme is read from swatch's own files.
A schedule slot that names a
.I kelvin
takes the colour dimension for itself; a slot without one lets the accent show.
.SH SETUP
.TP
.B setup
Fetch the device token from the Xiaomi cloud by QR code, then write it to the
configuration file. Interactive: it opens a QR image to be scanned with the
Xiaomi Home app. Needed once, and again only if the lamp is reset.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/lamp/config.toml
Device address, token, scenes, and rules. Contains a device credential and
should be mode 600.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/lamp/state.json
When the current manual override expires.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Logs/lamp.log
Launch agent errors.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.EX
ip = "192.168.1.4"
token = "0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef"

[scenes.read]
brightness = 80
kelvin = 4000

[scenes.sleep]
brightness = 5
rgb = "#ff3000"

[[schedule]]
from = "18:00"
brightness = 50

[[schedule]]
from = "23:00"
brightness = 25
kelvin = 2200

[media]
brightness = 30
.EE
.PP
The token is a 32 character hex string, written by
.BR "lamp setup" .
Omitting
.I schedule
entirely disables the reactive layer.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits non-zero if the configuration is missing or invalid, if the argument is
not understood, or if the lamp does not answer. A lamp that is switched off at
the wall is reported as unreachable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swatch (1)
